    "rain": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Transcribed from CAMPAIGN.md §5.1 / §12.2 '1-1'..'1-6' and corrected for KI1 (the lane limit): E4a0 352-864 has a 64-px lane (feet 161-224), E1a2 176-464 48 px (177-224), E1a0 928-1312 48 px (161-208) and the E7a0 512-1024 quay 48 px (113-160, over the canal), so CAMPAIGN's 'full band' pieces fail gates 2 and 3 as written.",
    "Test-safe start (gate 3 needs a band covering mid +-48, i.e. >= 97 px): the E4a0 pavement is extended toward the sea wall by copying its own floor cells (E4a0 h 16-64, the rows at y 176-224) up to y 112 with their terrain (type 0), so the lane 113-224 stands on scroll2 floor art over its whole height. A walk patch over the far layer (the first build) is not used any more.",
    "Other lanes: walk patches only over floor art (E1a2 sidewalk row y 161-176; E1a0 roof row y 145-160); gate 2 rejects a walk patch over a cell less than half opaque. The E7a0 quay becomes a promenade: E7a0 plaza slabs (E7a0 0-256, h 16-96, every other copy mirrored so the copies meet on mirror joins) replace its balustrade, wall and canal rows (y 144-224), giving a 112-px lane.",
    "1-1 order changed so the test-safe 640 px are one flat band: E4a0 352-864, E4a0 608-864 flip, E1a2 176-464, E4a0 352-640 (CAMPAIGN had the E1a2 join at 512, inside the 640 px gate 3 needs flat).",
    "Seams (CAMPAIGN §4.1 join chunks): every join of two different sources is covered by the harbor pillar, the brick jamb of the E7a0 arch (E7a0 1760-1792, palette row 27 lifted off the tunnel behind it; a full-height foreground pillar), centred on the join. Same-source joins are mirror joins.",
    "Far layer: one per section (CAMPAIGN §12.2, ARCHITECTURE §3.3): 1-1 the E4a0 sea wall (shift 1) behind every piece of the section, 1-2 the E7a0 city across the bay (shift 2), 1-3 the E4a2 factory (shift 2, amber), 1-4 the E7a0 bay, 1-5 the E1a0 sea (shift 3), 1-6 the E4a0 sea wall. Where it changes inside an area the change sits under a pillar.",
    "Palette: harbor-night on every scroll2 slice, with the 'stone' role given for E4a0, E7a0, E4a2 and E1a0 (all rows: the night scale keeps pens 1-3, the stone tint changes them too) so no slice keeps most of its 1993 colours (gate 4 counts recoloured pixels); E1a2 slices take the night scale without the kept window pens and the scroll3 skies take s3ops (night scale + 20% toward #1a2a5a); the sea borrow role is not given."
  ],
